{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:37f403c07733944d","name":"Droch Swarm","source":{"id":"source:reference-37f403c07733944d","title":"Droch Swarm","revision":20399,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:46:31Z","sha256":"af935c6af0cf325c94f169bed401a13e33cd83fc67d68273ab505edf7415838c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20399","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Droch%20Swarm&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-37f403c07733944d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Droch are plague-bearing insects from the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nam Chorios"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nam_Chorios?action=edit&redlink=1"},". Droch detect light from any source. When exposed, they become sluggish and infertile. The moment they are returned to darkness, however, they move quickly and reproduce at an alarming rate. As if this weren't bad enough, a Droch has the ability to burrow inside a host, rapidly killing it from the inside. The corpse then becomes a safe lair and a source of food for the Droch and its brood.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Droch Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Droch can be found almost anywhere, including abandoned buildings, tunnels, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},", provided the area is completely dark and there is access to food. For thousands of years, strict guidelines have been in place to keep Droch from spreading, but even draconian measures have not been sufficient to completely wipe out this dangerous vermin. A ship that has been exposed to a Droch infestation is usually blasted out of space before it can reach port.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Droch"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droc